.TH KEYKEY-SMART-PHRASES 1 "October 2026" "KeyKey" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keykey-smart-phrases \- manage Smart Mandarin custom phrases and learning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keykey-smart-phrases list
.br
.B keykey-smart-phrases add
.I phrase "reading"
.br
.B keykey-smart-phrases remove
.I phrase "reading"
.br
.B keykey-smart-phrases reset-learning

.SH DESCRIPTION
Readings use one space-separated Bopomofo syllable per character. Quote the
reading so the shell passes it as one argument. Candidate choices are learned
automatically while typing with Smart Mandarin. The reset-learning command
clears candidate and adjacent-word learning while preserving custom phrases.
.PP
All commands use the Guanyinma database.
.TP
.B list --json
Print custom phrases as a JSON array of objects with text, reading and qstring.
.TP
.B readings PHRASE
Read the installed model and custom phrases to print a JSON array of possible
Bopomofo readings. Results and per-character combinations are bounded to 64.
.TP
.B update OLD_PHRASE "OLD_READING" NEW_PHRASE "NEW_READING"
Atomically edit an existing Guanyinma custom phrase. Packaged dictionary entries
are read-only and cannot be edited.
.TP
.B export FILE.json
Write a complete Guanyinma JSON backup using a private temporary file and atomic
replacement. The model, Guanyinma database, their sidecars and aliases cannot
be backup destinations.
.TP
.B import FILE.json
Validate the entire archive before atomically importing it. Custom phrases merge;
provided Smart or table learning sections replace that domain. Missing learning
sections preserve existing data.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the private user database. Defaults to ~/.local/share.
.TP
.B CHICHI77_KEYKEY_GUANYINMA_USER_DB
Override the separate Guanyinma database path; defaults to
$XDG_DATA_HOME/chichi77-keykey/guanyinma-user.db.
.TP
.B CHICHI77_KEYKEY_DATA_DIR
Override the directory containing the read-only installed smart-mandarin.db.
